· Coordinate vehicle logistics from our manufacturers in China to the export ports;
· Organize and monitor sea freight from China to Europe;
· Follow vessels, shipments, ETDs, ETAs and vehicle arrivals;
· Coordinate vehicle reception and operations at European ports;
· Coordinate any required port operations, treatments, storage and vehicle release;
· Organize onward transportation from Europe to Switzerland;
· Coordinate final vehicle deliveries from Switzerland to our dealer partners;
· Ensure smooth coordination between all parties involved throughout the logistics
chain.

· Monitor the status and location of all vehicles throughout the entire logistics process;
· Maintain our internal vehicle tracking platform and ensure that all information iscontinuously and accurately updated;
· Track VINs, current location, logistics status, ETD, ETA, completed milestones andnext steps;
· Ensure that Sales, Operations and Management always have access to reliable and upto-date vehicle information;
· Proactively identify delays, inconsistencies or potential bottlenecks and take the necessary actions;
· Follow up with logistics providers and other stakeholders until issues are resolved;
· Coordinate priorities according to vehicle availability, customer orders and dealer requirements.

· Collect, verify and centralize logistics and transport documentation;
· Coordinate required documents with manufacturers, freight forwarders, ports and logistics providers;
· Ensure that vehicles and their corresponding documentation progress correctly through each stage of the logistics chain;
· Maintain clear and structured documentation for each shipment and vehicle;
· Communicate proactively with internal teams regarding delays, changes and important logistics developments.

· Contribute to the continuous improvement of our vehicle logistics processes;
· Help develop and optimize our internal logistics and vehicle tracking platform;
· Identify opportunities to automate repetitive logistics and reporting tasks;
· Improve the quality, reliability and accessibility of logistics data;
· Monitor logistics lead times, costs and supplier performance;
· Contribute to building a scalable logistics organization capable of supporting AM Group's continued growth.

· Education or professional experience in logistics, supply chain, international transportation, import/export or a related field;
· Previous experience in international logistics, maritime transport or freight forwarding is an advantage;
· Experience in the automotive industry, with an importer, manufacturer or logistics provider, is a strong advantage;
· Experience coordinating multiple international suppliers and logistics partners is appreciated.

· Excellent organizational and coordination skills;
· Strong ability to manage a large number of vehicles, shipments and stakeholders simultaneously;
· Very good command of English, both written and spoken, essential for daily communication with our manufacturers and international partners;
· French and/or German are important assets for communication within Switzerland;
· Very good IT skills and strong affinity with digital tools;
· Confident use of Excel and database or logistics management platforms;
· Comfortable using AI tools such as ChatGPT and interested in integrating automation and artificial intelligence into operational processes;
· Ability to structure, analyze and maintain large amounts of operational data accurately.

· Independent and solution-oriented;
· Highly organized and detail-oriented;
· Pragmatic and willing to take responsibility;
· Proactive – you identify potential problems before they become critical;
· Persistent when following up with suppliers and logistics partners;
· Comfortable working in an entrepreneurial environment where things move quickly;
· Curious and eager to continuously improve processes;
· Comfortable working in a multicultural and international environment.
